ogle made a smart choice to spend  money where matters and is most  noticeable the camera the display and  the speakers the things that you  actually interact with day to day as I  already mentioned the display the  speakers aren't as good as the pixel  threes but the oullette screen and  stereo speakers definitely get close and  fight way above their price point the  photo quality is really good basically  the same as the pixel threes the  algorithms have been tweaked over time  and I notice the images don't have the  same strong bias towards cool white  balances which I'm glad they tweaked  since we have  a single lens camera zoom shots are  still behind phones with a dedicated  telephoto lens but because of Google's  photo staff team it looks better than  other single systems like Dai Quentin  ours portrait photos oddly now use a 2 x  digital crop instead of the 1.25 times  the pixel 3 use I really like the slight  crop of the pixel 3 a limited distortion  for close-ups but still gave a high  quality great looking wide portrait  video recording is still a few years  behind the flagships with no 4k 60 and  poor mic quality but that's passable at  this price point the main takeaway is  that this phone will take better  standard photos than any phone under  $500 and many that are far more  expensive my only other complaint is the  shutter lag it seems worse than the  pixel 3 and far behind the flagships and  this side-by-side i press a shutter  right when Ilan was at the top of the  swing the iPhone grab the image  instantly every single time since it's  actually consistently taking photos and  just saves the photo when you press the  Samsung and oneplus are behind but  nowhere near as much as a 3a XL which  took the image almost a second later I  complained about this in my sm+ review  since I noticed myself missing shots on  my kids in action which I probably  wouldn't have with iPhone if you have  little kids pets or shoot other quick  moving subjects this could 